  "summary_en": "Editorial introducing an AI & Society special issue applying Martin Buber's I-Thou and dialogical philosophy to robotics and AI ethics. It questions instrumental conceptions of relationship in social robotics and chatbots, and warns of dehumanisation. It summarises the contributions; it proposes no regulation.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Robotics and AI research often construes relationships instrumentally, rooted in an egocentric Western tradition.",
   "Humans are never tools; Buber's I-Thou offers an alternative model of relationship.",
   "Contributors differ on whether I-Thou relations with artificial agents are possible.",
   "Dehumanisation concerns are neglected in current robotics and AI narratives."
